# ---------------------------------------------------------------- build ----
rust/target/
third_party/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ------------------------------------------------------------ reference ----
# Reference material read while writing this engine, cloned separately and
# not part of what meteor-cfd distributes. See NOTICE.
reference/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- cases ----
# Every case here is GENERATED by `ofgpu-generate-mesh`, and the meshes and
# results run to hundreds of megabytes. Regenerate rather than clone:
#
#   cargo run --release --bin ofgpu-generate-mesh -- channel  ../cases/channel  200 120 1
#   cargo run --release --bin ofgpu-generate-mesh -- cavity   ../cases/cavity    80  80 1
#   cargo run --release --bin ofgpu-generate-mesh -- damBreak ../cases/damBreak  60 100 1
#
# ...but the .jsonc case DEFINITIONS are the opposite of generated data: a
# few kB of text each, referenced by docs/07-lowmach-solver.md and by
# ofgpu-validate, and without them a fresh clone can reproduce nothing.
cases/*
!cases/README.md
!cases/*.jsonc
# The race-car sample is a geometry and a recipe, not a mesh: 52 kB of STL and
# the two commands that turn it into a 2.1-million-cell run. The mesh and the
# results it produces are a gigabyte, and they are what the user's own machine
# is for.
!cases/racecar.stl
!cases/racecar.md
!cases/racecar.cmd
# Retired case definitions - kept as dated records of measurements that were
# taken before a later SPEC-LIT rule made the cases themselves unrunnable.
# They are records, not cases; cases/retired/README.md says what replaced each.
!cases/retired/

# ------------------------------------------------------------- results -----
*.png
*.mp4

# ------------------------------------------------------------ packaging ----
# Built installers. `packaging/iterations.iss` is the recipe; the output is not
# part of the source tree - it belongs to a GitHub release.
/dist/
